    "q-118692": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118692",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14187003/assets/5548481ccbe3aee88fd4b346ad53777b7101223c19f7e8408c8ef85bb0d9df25.png)\n\nGiven the right triangle $△PQR$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $Q$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{PR},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PR}.$\n\nThe correct diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14187003/assets/301c31fa98ce5c016337f422566b94a742e3da126b76f9060e4b13d6a8e86358.png)",
