    "q-77607": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77607",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14187003/assets/ef5b44834fba3ae32b6f77a343907f10becb2d06d356ec1c244d265530ffb2a7.png)\n\nGiven $△ABC$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AB}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $C$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{AB},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14187003/assets/78721c4365703d4511dcf9d90659034c9aa8eaa980e8c37c7bb0c2068e9eccba.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $C$ to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14187003/assets/3ff8df9df6788053548ddcb092265ebb1af89f06512bb6052f0f7d8225e03c71.png)",
