    "q-118759": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118759",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14187003/assets/d53e300cf45128d4d0d3e06e9c4adc6ab966ff9493c399496d18a2e2bf634099.png)\n\nConsider $△PQR$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{RH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PQ}.$ If $m∠PQR={105}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠QRH.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HQR+m∠PQR & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HQR+{105}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HQR & ={75}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△QHR$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QRH+m∠HQR+m∠RHQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH+{75}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH+{165}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH & ={15}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
